# total() runs once and only calls what it is handed, so boot() may make that arrow in its own frame. The closure inside captures the parameter. (What install() is handed goes on to a list: nobody lends it.)
# Left out, it would be stored into a word that outlives the frame. A parameter that is only called is the source of no word: it stays a capture, which brings it to the heap where a heap closure takes it.
